# Every text file checks out as LF, on every platform, regardless of what the
# person cloning has set for core.autocrlf.
#
# THE BREAKAGE THIS PREVENTS, measured 2026-08-21.  This repository is checked
# out with core.autocrlf=false, so its working tree is LF.  A fresh clone on
# Windows inherits Git-for-Windows' default core.autocrlf=true, converts the
# whole tree to CRLF on checkout, and `python -m build` then packs those CRLF
# bytes into the artefact.  The wheel built from the clean clone shipped a
# LICENSE of 11,063 bytes where this tree's is 10,861 -- same text, 202 CRLF
# bytes of difference, different SHA-256.  NOTICE moved the same way, 5,235
# against 5,135.
#
# So without this file the built distribution's bytes depend on who cloned it
# and on what platform, including the two files whose whole job is to state the
# licence.  A licence file that hashes differently per builder cannot be pinned,
# and `dist-info/licenses/` is exactly where a downstream consumer looks.
#
# The digests this now holds to, in the repository, in the sdist, inside the
# wheel's dist-info/licenses/, and in a venv the wheel was installed into --
# proven equal across all four from a clone made with core.autocrlf=true:
#
#   LICENSE  8e2a44ae339215e85e0fad7d8f0acb0d0ef91cf07ba8d215d85ef858eef8de9a
#   NOTICE   9caa80d56d0e2bb8ea9d0d81117a575166eeabbbca7979979d207e8e517a1d9c
#
# Before this file existed the same clone produced a wheel whose LICENSE hashed
# 7266f9cb821da0680f6e421e905506fa1ae8c8c5159ffffc3ebe1262f21650fe instead.
#
# LICENSE is Apache-2.0 verbatim and does not move.  NOTICE does: it carries
# the derivative marking and the declared divergences, so it is restated
# whenever those are.  Re-measure it at a cut rather than trusting this line.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect and leave alone anything genuinely binary.
# Measured when this file was added: 181 tracked files, zero of them binary,
# one stored with CRLF (tools/probe_partition_residency_v841.py), renormalised
# in the same commit.  The count is a record of that measurement, not a claim
# about the current tree, which grows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF or they do not run at all; state it rather than
# relying on the wildcard above surviving an edit.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Byte-pinned scientific data, if any ever lands here, is never line-ending
# converted.  netCDF and NumPy payloads are pinned by SHA-256 across the port's
# proof guards, and one substituted byte is a failed pin.
*.nc    binary
*.npy   binary
*.npz   binary
*.rwg   binary
